</section>

<!-- INTRODUCTION SECTION -->
<section class="acdt-intro content-section" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
  <h2 id="intro-heading" class="sr-only">About GMT to PST Conversion</h2>
  <p>
    Welcome to the definitive <strong>GMT to PST Converter</strong>. When coordinating communication between Europe's primary financial capital in London and the global center of technological innovation in Silicon Valley, understanding the <strong>8-hour time gap</strong> between Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) and Pacific Standard Time (PST) is paramount. Greenwich Mean Time functions as the astronomical reference line at Coordinated Universal Time +0 (UTC+0), while Pacific Standard Time operates at UTC-8. As a result, Pacific Standard Time is exactly 8 hours behind Greenwich Mean Time.
  </p>
  <p>
    This substantial 8-hour time gap creates unique scheduling dynamics. When professionals in London or Dublin are concluding their workday at 5:00 PM GMT, software engineers and business leaders in Los Angeles, San Francisco, Seattle, and Vancouver are just starting their morning at 9:00 AM PST. Navigating this narrow overlap window requires precise calculation to prevent missed meetings, erroneous product launches, or misaligned server deployment schedules.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our web application delivers instant calculation using official IANA database keys (`UTC` and `America/Los_Angeles`). Whether you manage remote development teams across the Atlantic, coordinate entertainment industry distribution, organize gaming tournaments, or schedule cross-border logistics, this guide provides dual live clocks, full 24-hour conversion matrices, meeting overlap strategies, and complete regional breakdowns.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     CONVERTER COMPONENT & HERO GRAPHIC
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
