      <rect x="100" y="20" width="12" height="120" fill="#1b536e" />
      <!-- Main Suspension Cables -->
      <path d="M 0 60 Q 26 120 60 120 Q 94 120 120 60" fill="none" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="2" />
      <!-- Roadway -->
      <rect x="-10" y="110" width="150" height="8" fill="#2f6278" />
      <text x="65" y="165" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">San Francisco / PST</text>
    </g>

    <!-- Ground baseline -->
    <rect x="0" y="190" width="800" height="10" fill="#071b26" />
    <line x1="0" y1="190" x2="800" y2="190" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="2" />
  </svg>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     TIME DIFFERENCE MECHANICS SECTION
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section" id="time-difference" aria-labelledby="time-diff-heading">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Mathematical Mechanics</p>
    <h2 id="time-diff-heading">Analyzing the 8-Hour Gap: GMT vs PST</h2>
    <p>
      The relationship between Greenwich Mean Time and Pacific Standard Time is governed by an <strong>8-hour offset difference</strong>. GMT sits at UTC+0 while PST sits at UTC-8. To convert GMT to PST, simply subtract 8 hours from the GMT time:
    </p>
    <p style="text-align: center; font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: bold; color: var(--accent); background: var(--panel); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--line);">
      PST Time = GMT Time − 8 Hours
    </p>
    <p>
      Because 8 hours is one-third of a full day, morning events in GMT correspond to late night or early pre-dawn hours in PST, whereas late afternoon events in GMT occur during the PST morning start of day.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- SIDE-BY-SIDE GRAPHIC -->
