    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>1. Direct Math Rule</h3>
      <p>Subtract 8 from any GMT hour. If the hour drops below zero, add 24 to get the Pacific clock hour and step back one calendar day.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>2. The Late Afternoon Overlap</h3>
      <p>The only practical overlap window during regular workdays falls between 4:00 PM and 7:00 PM GMT, which equates to 8:00 AM to 11:00 AM PST.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>3. Seasonal Clock Shifts</h3>
      <p>When the UK enters BST (UTC+1) and the US West Coast enters PDT (UTC-7), the relative difference between local clocks remains 8 hours.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

