     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="content-section" id="dst-explained">
  <h2>Daylight Saving Time Dynamics: GMT/BST vs PST/PDT</h2>
  <p>
    Understanding Daylight Saving Time between the UK and North America's Pacific Coast requires paying attention to transition dates. While both regions shift their clocks by 1 hour, the start and end dates differ:
  </p>

  <!-- SVG DST Diagram -->
  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 750px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 700 200" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="700" height="200" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      
      <g transform="translate(30, 40)">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="35" rx="6" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" />
        <text x="15" y="22" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#f4fbff">Winter (Standard Time):</text>
        <text x="220" y="22" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#36c7b5">GMT (UTC+0) vs PST (UTC-8)</text>
        <text x="540" y="22" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#8fd7ff">8 Hours Gap</text>
      </g>

      <g transform="translate(30, 90)">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="35" rx="6" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" />
        <text x="15" y="22" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#f4fbff">Summer (Daylight Time):</text>
        <text x="220" y="22" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#36c7b5">BST (UTC+1) vs PDT (UTC-7)</text>
        <text x="540" y="22" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#8fd7ff">8 Hours Gap</text>
      </g>

      <g transform="translate(30, 140)">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="40" rx="6" fill="#1b536e" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="15" y="25" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#36c7b5">Spring/Fall Discrepancy Window:</text>
        <text x="220" y="25" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#f4fbff">US shifts 2 weeks earlier in March / 1 week later in Nov</text>
        <text x="540" y="25" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#36c7b5">7 or 9 Hours Gap</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <p>
    During the transition window in mid-to-late March (after the US switches to PDT but before the UK switches to BST), the time difference reduces to <strong>7 hours</strong>. Conversely, in late October (after the UK reverts to GMT but before the US reverts to PST), the gap briefly expands to <strong>9 hours</strong>.
  </p>
</section>

