      <h3>Pacific Standard Time (PST) Regions</h3>
      <p>
        PST covers the Pacific coastline of North America, including major US states (California, Washington, Oregon, Nevada), the Canadian province of British Columbia, and northern Baja California in Mexico. Key urban centers include Los Angeles, San Francisco, Seattle, San Jose, and Vancouver.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Global Tech Infrastructure</h3>
      <p>
        Cloud platforms (AWS, Google Cloud, Azure) connect data center regions in London (`eu-west-2`) with Northern California (`us-west-1`) and Oregon (`us-west-2`). System administrators rely on precise GMT to PST translation for maintenance windows.
      </p>
    </article>
